Description:
  Records every Rack::Attack refusal as a Security::AbuseEvent in its own
  `security` database and shows the last week on a backstage page.

  Installs the maquina:rack_attack rules unless the initializer already
  defines Rack::Attack.banned?, plus the recording subscriber, models,
  db/security_schema.rb, the `security` database entries, a daily purge in
  config/recurring.yml, and the controller, layout, views, route and admin
  navigation tab. The page is behind the backstage Basic Auth and answers
  503 until credentials are set.

Examples:
  rails g maquina:security --prefix /admin
  rails g maquina:security --prefix /admin --login-path /sign_in
  rails g maquina:security --prefix /admin --no-copy-views
